@startuml epoch-reclamation
' ============================================================================
' Epoch-Based Reclamation (EBR) — why a cold node can be reclaimed during
' eviction WITHOUT a use-after-free under lock-free reads.
'
' Source of truth:
'   src/persistent_artrie/core/concurrency.rs (EpochManager:
'     enter_read / exit_read / advance / has_active_readers /
'     wait_for_quiescence — note the SeqCst StoreLoad fence rationale),
'   src/persistent_artrie/core/eviction/coordinator.rs (wait_for_quiescence
'     then the unswizzle callback), and
'   src/persistent_artrie/core/swizzled_ptr.rs (unswizzle = the atomic swap).
'
' THE GUARANTEE: the eviction thread advances the epoch, then HOLDS the free
' until every reader that could still hold a raw pointer into the victim has
' departed (quiescence). A reader that arrives AFTER the boundary either
' re-faults the node from disk or follows the already-published DiskRef, so it
' never dereferences freed memory.
'
' Color key:
'   green (#C8E6C9) = reader inside an epoch (may hold a live raw node pointer)
'   amber (#FFE0B2) = eviction-thread control (advance · wait · select)
'   red   (#FFCDD2) = the reclamation point (free) — only safe after quiescence
'   blue  (#BBDEFB) = the durable on-disk side (DiskRef the victim leaves behind)
'   grey  (#ECEFF1) = the shared EBR counters (global_epoch, active_readers)
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #37474F
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #90A4AE
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #F9A825
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #ECEFF1
skinparam noteBorderColor #90A4AE
skinparam participantBorderColor #37474F

title Epoch-based reclamation — defer the free until old-epoch readers depart (no use-after-free)

participant "Reader A\n(old epoch)" as RA #C8E6C9
participant "Reader B\n(arrives later)" as RB #C8E6C9
participant "EBR counters\nglobal_epoch · active_readers" as E #ECEFF1
participant "Eviction thread" as EV #FFE0B2
participant "Victim node\n→ DiskRef" as N #BBDEFB

== Reader A enters and pins the current epoch ==
RA -> E : enter_read()\nactive_readers.fetch_add(1, **SeqCst**)
activate RA
E --> RA : epoch = 5 (Acquire load)
note right of RA #C8E6C9
  A now follows a **swizzled** child pointer at
  native speed and may hold a raw `*const Node`
  into the victim. The SeqCst pin publishes
  BEFORE any pointer A subsequently loads.
end note

== Eviction thread opens an epoch boundary ==
EV -> E : advance()\nglobal_epoch 5 → 6
activate EV
EV -> E : has_active_readers()? (**SeqCst** load)
note over EV, E #FFE0B2
  wait_for_quiescence: the SeqCst load pairs with A's
  SeqCst pin (StoreLoad fence). If the scan misses A,
  A is guaranteed to observe the unlink and re-fault —
  AcqRel alone would NOT close this gap.
end note
E --> EV : **true** — Reader A still active
note right of EV #FFE0B2 : DEFER the free.\nSlow path: block on the quiescence condvar\n(bounded by quiescence_timeout).

... Reader A is still walking the victim subtree ...

== Reader A finishes and leaves the epoch ==
RA -> E : exit_read()\nactive_readers.fetch_sub(1, **SeqCst**)
note left of RA #C8E6C9 : A's pointer accesses are globally ordered\nBEFORE this un-pin, so a reclaimer that now\nsees the count hit 0 knows A is done.
deactivate RA
E -> EV : last reader left → condvar.notify_all()
E --> EV : has_active_readers() == **false** → quiescence reached

== Quiescent: now the swap + free are safe ==
EV -> N : unswizzle(block_id, location, type)\natomic CAS: ChildNode → DiskRef
activate N
N --> EV : Ok(old_ptr) — the in-memory node is unlinked
hnote over N #FFCDD2 : **free(old_ptr)** — reclaim the RAM.\nNo live reader can still reach it.
deactivate N
deactivate EV

== A reader that arrives AFTER the boundary is always safe ==
RB -> E : enter_read()  → epoch = 6
activate RB
RB -> N : follow child pointer
note right of RB #BBDEFB
  B observes the **already-published DiskRef** (the swap
  preceded the free) and faults the node back in from
  disk — it never touches the freed allocation.
end note
RB -> E : exit_read()
deactivate RB

note across #FFF9C4
  EBR in one line: **advance → wait for quiescence → swap → free.**
  The free is delayed until no thread from the pre-boundary epoch can hold a
  pointer to the victim, which is exactly what lets eviction run concurrently
  with lock-free, lock-free-fast readers.
end note
@enduml
